From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: restart a job's termination from the head after each
 process

terminate_job walked the job's processes with a saved next entry. Ending
one closes its handles, and a process of the job that had already ended
and was kept alive only by such a handle is then destroyed, which takes
it off the list: the saved entry pointed at freed memory and
`assert( process->job == job )` failed, which on iOS ends the app with
every process of its session. The Rockstar Games Launcher installer, a
Steam prerequisite that Playport closed after its time limit, had
started winemenubuilder.exe, which had ended.

Walk from the head after each process instead, skipping those already
terminating, as kill_console_processes does.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-15-rockstar-stage0-phone.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 server/process.c | 17 +++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/server/process.c b/server/process.c
index c8b97b8..23ddab4 100644
--- a/server/process.c
+++ b/server/process.c
@@ -318,7 +318,7 @@ static void release_job_process( struct process *process )
 
 static void terminate_job( struct job *job, int exit_code )
 {
-    struct process *process, *next_process;
+    struct process *process;
     struct job *j, *next_job;
 
     LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY_SAFE( j, next_job, &job->child_job_list, struct job, parent_job_entry )
@@ -330,11 +330,20 @@ static void terminate_job( struct job *job, int exit_code )
         release_object( j );
     }
 
+    /* Restart from the head after each process: ending one closes its handles, and
+     * a process that already ended and was kept only by such a handle (a child the
+     * job's process started) is then destroyed and leaves the list, so a saved next
+     * entry may be gone. */
     job->terminating = 1;
-    LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY_SAFE( process, next_process, &job->process_list, struct process, job_entry )
+    for (;;)
     {
-        assert( process->job == job );
-        if (process->running_threads) terminate_process( process, NULL, exit_code );
+        LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY( process, &job->process_list, struct process, job_entry )
+        {
+            assert( process->job == job );
+            if (process->running_threads && !process->is_terminating) break;
+        }
+        if (&process->job_entry == &job->process_list) break;
+        terminate_process( process, NULL, exit_code );
     }
     job->terminating = 0;
     signal_sync( job->sync );
